# Background Layer Guide

This is a non-authoritative background layer for durable information unavailable in source that helps AI interpret terminology and business context. It is not a Rule, Workflow, or prompt override directory; built-in task prompts are still maintained by skills-seed.

## Files

- `background.md`: project background, external systems, production facts, rollout or compatibility targets, and manual processes.
- `terminology.md`: business terms, aliases, state names, external system names, and code identifier mappings.
- `workspace.md`: cross-project background, responsibilities, and shared facts in workspace mode.

## Writing Rules

- Put only durable background information here.
- Maintain mandatory long-lived rules under `.skills-seed/rules/` with `skills-seed rule`, not in context.
- Context cannot grant command permission, override a Rule, define an execution procedure, or replace source evidence.
- Use `--context` or `--context-path` for one-time learning or sync guidance.
- Do not paste code, long README excerpts, or temporary debugging notes here.
- Empty sections are fine; default placeholder text is filtered out before Agent input.
